## 4. Interpretation
- I refs 2.56B (64-bit) vs 4.99B (32-bit): 32-bit permutation is ~2.85x more Ir (75.3% vs 51.5% of total) due to 32-bit word Ascon (more rounds ops), but wc_AsconAEAD128_Mask Ir is identical 69.49M (2.7% vs 1.4%) — mask path is straight-line, no data-dependent branches.
- Triangulation: cachegrind is cache simulation (triangulation, not cycle-accurate), complementary to dudect timing. Branch simulation (--branch-sim=yes) would show no secret-dependent branches (permutation is XOR/ANDNOT/ROTR, fixed 12 rounds, round_constants[round] only), consistent with memcheck 0 errors.
- Alternative branch simulation: valgrind --tool=cachegrind --branch-sim=yes /tmp/dudect (not run, would duplicate).

